# Three-layer policy enforcement for the authorization-code flow.
#
# Render
# ------
# ``d2 --theme=0 --pad=20 assets/diagrams/policy-flow.d2 \
#       assets/diagrams/policy-flow.svg``
#
# or via the nox session::
#
#     uv run nox -s diagrams
#
# The session is opt-in — same skip-with-warning pattern as
# ``markdown_lint`` / ``actions_lint``. ``d2`` is a single Go binary;
# install via the official script (https://d2lang.com/install.sh) or
# https://github.com/terrastruct/d2 releases. Re-render after any
# edit and commit both source (.d2) and output (.svg) — the CI's
# ``diagrams-fresh`` step asserts the SVG is in sync with the source.

shape: sequence_diagram

RP: Relying Party
Auth: AuthAuthorizationView (views.py)
DOT: django-oauth-toolkit
Token: TokenView (views.py)
V: AllianceAuthOAuth2Validator (auth_provider.py)
AP: AccessPolicy.pkce_required (security.py)

"Layer 1 — views.py:dispatch() runs on GET *and* POST": {
  RP -> Auth: GET/POST /o/authorize/\nresponse_type=code
  Auth -> Auth: check global access_oidc\n+ state/group whitelist
  Auth -> DOT: forward (policy passes)
  DOT -> AP: pkce_required(client_id)\nvia OAUTH2_PROVIDER callable
  AP -> DOT: True / False (per-app)
  DOT -> DOT: enforce PKCE per resolver\n(reject if required and missing)
  DOT -> RP: 302 redirect with auth code
}

"Layer 2 — auth_provider.py:validate_code() / validate_refresh_token()": {
  RP -> Token: POST /o/token/\ncode + client_secret
  Token -> V: validate_code(code, request)
  V -> V: re-check state/group\non exchange
  V -> Token: ok / invalid_grant
}

"Layer 3 — auth_provider.py:save_bearer_token() — last guard": {
  Token -> V: save_bearer_token(...)
  V -> V: PermissionDenied\n→ InvalidGrantError
  V -> RP: 200 access_token + id_token
}
